# Reverse proxy + automatic TLS in front of integrations/serve_production.py.
#
# Caddy chosen over nginx specifically for this project: it provisions
# and renews a real Let's Encrypt certificate automatically just from
# the domain name below -- no separate certbot setup, no manual renewal
# cron job. Runs the same way on Windows as on Mac/Linux.
#
# Setup, once you have a real domain pointed at this server's public IP:
#   1. Replace the placeholder domain below with your real one.
#   2. Install Caddy (https://caddyserver.com/docs/install) -- there's
#      a Windows installer, no compilation needed.
#   3. Make sure integrations/serve_production.py is already running
#      (it must be listening on 127.0.0.1:5000 before Caddy starts).
#   4. Run: caddy run --config deploy/Caddyfile
#
# Point Telnyx's webhook URLs (SMS webhook, voice assistant tools) at
# https://your-real-domain.example.com/... -- never at the bare
# 127.0.0.1:5000 address, which isn't reachable from the internet and
# isn't meant to be.

your-real-domain.example.com {
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5000
}
